  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000124043,
      "SummaryText": "Lone Star Beef Processors operates a beef processing facility in San Angelo, Texas. The facility operates an ammonia refrigeration system to provide cooling and freezing capabilities. We have a strong commitment to operate our facility in a safe and responsible manner.\n\nAmmonia is used at our facility as the cooling and freezing medium in our refrigeration system. The ammonia is contained in a closed loop system; it is designed to remain inside the piping and vessels in our facility. We believe that ammonia provides the safest and most efficient cooling choice for our operation.\n\nA. Accident Release Prevention and Emergency Policies\n\nWe take many precautions to prevent or minimize accidental releases of ammonia from the refrigeration system. These precautions include safety controls (alarms and automatic shutdown devices) which are designed to identify and prevent potentially unsafe conditions like pressure increases that could cause a system failure. We have a preventative maintenance program designed to maintain the on-going integrity of the systems, a training program designed to ensure that the systems are operated by qualified personnel, and emergency response procedures that enable trained personnel to respond to system upsets.\n\n\nB. Stationary Source and Regulated Substances Handled\n\nAmmonia is the only substance covered by the Accidental Release Prevention Regulations handled at this facility.\n\n\nC. Description of the Accidental Release Prevention Program\n\nThe facility has an accident release prevention program that complies with Occupational Safety and Health Act\u0092s Process Safety Management Standard and EPA\u0092s Risk Management Program Rule. The prevention program consists of the following elements:\n\n\u00b7 Employee Participation Program\n\u00b7 Process Safety Information\n\u00b7 Process Hazard Analysis\n\u00b7 Operating Procedures\n\u00b7 Training Program\n\u00b7 Contractor Safety Program\n\u00b7 Pre-Startup Safety Review Procedures\n\u00b7 Mechanical Integrity Program\n\u00b7 Hot Work Permit Procedures\n\u00b7 Managem"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000124043,
      "SummaryText": "ent of Change Procedures\n\u00b7 Incident Investigation Procedures\n\u00b7 Compliance Audit Procedures\n\nD. Five Year Accident History\n\nNo ammonia-related accidents have occurred at the facility over the past five years that resulted in significant onsite or offsite consequences.\n\nE. Description of the Emergency Response Program\n\nAn emergency response program has been implemented at the facility. This program contains procedures describing how the facility will respond to ammonia spills and other emergencies, including evacuation procedures. The program has been coordinated with local fire department officials and the LEPC.\n\nF. Planned Changes to Improve Safety\n\nWe have identified no potential changes to improve the safety of our ammonia refrigeration system.\n\nNote To EPA:\nThe previous RMP submission (2020), listed 45,000 lbs. of ammonia based on design system capacity.  The current submission (2025) corrects this to reflect the actual maximum inventory of 24,000 lbs. of ammonia required to operate the system. This submittal updates the maximum quantity of ammonia based on verified operational data. No significant process changes have occurred other than this correction. All prevention, emergency response and safety programs remain in place and compliant with EPA and OSHA requirements."
    }
  ]
